WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.134 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.035 line:92%
We were just talking backstage.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.804
We've met a couple of times
because you hosted "SNL" and --

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
or you didn't host,
but you were a musical guest

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:08.341 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in 2010 and 2011.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.943 size:81% position:41%
You don't do a lot of
talking on talk shows?

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:15.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I get really nervous
and I get quite shy, so, yeah.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:16.383 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-All right.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.484 size:75% position:38%
-I get a bit scared,
but I'm gonna try.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.388 line:92%
Well, one thing you did -- Yeah.

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.322 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this wasn't unique
to this show.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess you do this
all the time.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:28.628
But I went to the dressing room
to say hello before the show.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the same dressing room
every night.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:33.900
It doesn't look any different,
except tonight when I walked in,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.102 line:92%
you had completely redecorated.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.071 line:92%
There were a lot of scarves.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:41.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I moved the mirror
around a bit.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And yeah, I have --

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, I have quite
a strong sense of aesthetic.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if that comes across.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.551
When you walk into a room
that no one has touched

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:55.422
and you've completely rearranged
it, it came across.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.589 --> 00:01:00.593
-Some people say it's obsessive,
but I'm working on it.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:04.264
-Obsessive would be, if I called
you after you left and was like,

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You didn't put it back
exactly right."

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:07.567 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-But it looks better.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.170
-Well, it -- Okay.
It looks a little better, yeah.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that's something you do
when you are on tour?

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.141
-Yeah.
I mean, we bring -- well, yeah.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.976 size:78% position:39%
I bring -- I kind of
collect throws and --

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's lots of patterns
and embroidery and, kind of --

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.382
but it's also a nice thing to do
when you arrive and, you know,

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:25.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
I spend, like, a good
half an hour just kind of

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:25.985 line:92%
decorating and something.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:30.123
-Can you go over to friends'
houses and leave it alone?

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.024 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's hard, no.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.760 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I stay at home a lot.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wish that was a joke.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.632
-Well, you, obviously, you can't
stay home all the time

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you're going out
on tour.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:44.137
Australia, New Zealand -- you
are coming here to the States.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're doing the Barclays.
-Yes.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.273 line:92%
-So, do you like the road?

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.041 line:92%
Do you like the big shows?

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:52.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The shows are kind of --
it's just so important to me.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's where everything
comes together.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
It's kind of, like,

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
how I make sense of myself,
in a way.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:03.289
But also, I feel kind of -- I've
been doing it for a while,

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I feel kind of
really honored,

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause sometimes
you really get to see

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
the best in people at a show.
-Sure.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, you -- I mean, I
literally, I'm up there like,

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.899
"Everybody, tell each other
that you love each other.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell people you don't know
you love each other."

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:18.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you just see everybody,
they're so up for it.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And, yeah.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.974
So, it -- it, kind of -- it's so
important to me,

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
the live aspect and connection
is such a big part of that.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:27.180
And when you feel you're taking
everyone somewhere with you.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.716
It's a very collaborative thing,
I think, a gig.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:32.852
-And it must be nice, obviously,
to now be known.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I'm sure
in your early gigs,

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:35.655 line:92%
people didn't know who you were,

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.324
and if you told them to go tell
each other they love each other,

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:41.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're like, "That weird lady
is being very bossy."

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:41.861 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:45.031
-I don't know.
I was very drunk most of these.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was definitely
still being bossy.

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:51.971 size:84% position:42%
I don't think I minded
if people didn't do it.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:52.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, that's cute.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.274 line:92%
But this is -- very early on,

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
you knew you wanted to
be a performer.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is not something
you came to late in life.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've heard --
I should say I've read that

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.181 line:92%
when you were 8 years old,

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:05.618
you would put on your mom's
robes and sing Billie Holiday

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a wine glass
full of orange juice.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.923 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.090 line:92%
So, you -- you were, what, like,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
you wanted all of rock music
early on.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:13.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:17.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "I know
what I'm gonna be,

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:21.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it involves drinking
and being sad."

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.602 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.404 line:92%
And, you know, I went there.

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:25.305 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:25.738 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.807
You know, it's nice when
an 8-year-old finds their dream.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:31.744
-I was, like, 8 and I knew that
it would involve a wine glass.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, my God.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also, as an 8-year-old,
being like,

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Billie Holiday --
That's someone who gets me."

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
Billie Holiday, like,
Etta James, Nina Simone,

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, those were --
those were the first voices

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.057 line:92%
that I was really drawn to.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:44.691 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's fantastic.

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:48.294
I always, I remember, you know,
the first time I heard you sing,

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.896
and I also remember hearing
the band name and being like,

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:53.866
"Wow. Florence and the Machine,
that's a fantastic band name."

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.068 line:92%
It was not your first band.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it maybe was
your first good band name.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.139 line:92%
What was your first band?

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:03.042 line:92%
-My first band was at school.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.310 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I was 11,

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had a punk band called
The Toxic Cockroaches.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.450 line:92%
-But we only had a drum kit.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was the guitarist,
but I didn't have a guitar.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.688 size:84% position:42%
And the only instrument
we had was a drum kit.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:19.559
-Okay, so, what does a guitarist
without a guitar hold?

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.461 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not much.
-Yeah.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:23.896 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, not much.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.531 line:92%
I held a lot of enthusiasm.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's good. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.602 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.804 size:88% position:44% line:92%
That comes across today.

